   "heme_iron_biomass_terms": "m1635[C_cy] 1e-06 mmol/gDW; m948[C_cy] 3.04e-05 mmol/gDW",
   "lipoylation_growth_dilution": "LIPOYLATION-MODULE-20261020: alpha 1e-05 mmol/gDW each for lipoyl-H-protein and lipoyl-E2, apo forms returned; user-selected provisional value; no Yarrowia lipolytica measurement found; sensitivity at 1e-6, 1e-5, 1e-4",
   "tpp_requirement_authorization": "2026-10-22 user: Approved: implement the TPP plan as written: --tpp-requirement on top of cf0825b8, TPP in biomass_C at the yeast-GEM value 1.2e-6 mmol/gDW, R1342 closed (not deleted), ThiL BLAST check, KO comparison included. No commit or push.",
   "tpp_requirement_curation_id": "TPP-REQUIREMENT-20261022",
   "tpp_requirement_evidence": "yeast-GEM 9.1.1 cofactor pseudoreaction r_4598 consumes s_1475, named TDP (thiamine diphosphate: KEGG C00068, BiGG thmpp, C12H16N4O7P2S), at 1.2e-6 mmol/gDW; https://github.com/SysBioChalmers/yeast-GEM/blob/main/model/yeast-GEM.yml (raw file SHA-256 2ddfaaa73ead41ab243127d1b34fa56db2c86052f6eabcd12bb4eea93947dc17, read 2026-10-22)",
   "tpp_requirement_evidence_tier": "coefficient verified in yeast-GEM 9.1.1 on 2026-10-22; it is an S. cerevisiae value, not measured in Y. lipolytica, and is provisional. That TPP is a required cofactor (pyruvate dehydrogenase, 2-oxoglutarate dehydrogenase, transketolase, pyruvate decarboxylase) is established/uncited. m975 has no formula or cross-reference; its identity as thiamine diphosphate is inferred from its reactions R752 (KEGG R00619), R753 (KEGG R00616) and R933 (thiamine diphosphate transport).",
   "tpp_requirement_previous_state": "biomass_C had no TPP term",
   "tpp_requirement_rationale": "No reaction drained cytosolic TPP (m975) to a sink: its consumers R753 (to thiamine triphosphate, m976) and R933 (into mitochondria, m1116) end in dead ends. So TPP synthesis and THI80 (R752) carried no flux and a THI80 knockout had no effect. Diluting TPP into new biomass makes its synthesis required, as yeast-GEM does for TDP.",
   "tpp_requirement_status": "user_authorized_biomass_term_and_closure",
   "trehalose_biomass_authorization": "2026-10-30 user: Approve C on e1e7c868 (reports/trehalose_biomass_20261030 TASK.md section 9: trehalose m294[C_cy] removed from biomass_C, flag --trehalose-biomass-removal; option D, the R143 rule, deferred to its own round). No commit or push.",
   "trehalose_biomass_curation_id": "TREHALOSE-BIOMASS-20261030",
   "trehalose_biomass_evidence": "Flores et al. 2011, PLoS One, PMID 21931609, PMC3171402 (full text): Y. lipolytica wild type contains below 1 nmol trehalose per mg dry weight in minimal glucose medium (Table 4; per Methods, YNB without amino acids and ammonium sulfate plus 0.1 percent glutamate, generally 2 percent glucose, 30 C), and below 1 when grown in glucose up to stationary phase or in glycerol. The tps1 disruptant (YlTPS1 = YALI0E14685g = YALI1E17616g, UniProt O74932, cDNA AJ011032) grows on glucose at least as fast as the wild type (doubling time 139 vs 149 min); no trehalose is detected in tps1 with nth1 also disrupted or after heat shock (the content of the single tps1 mutant at 30 C is not reported). Trehalose is therefore not an obligate biomass component under this condition. Report reports/trehalose_biomass_20261030.",
   "trehalose_biomass_evidence_tier": "direct Y. lipolytica measurement (an upper bound: reported as below 1 nmol/mg DW; the paper states no detection limit) plus a Y. lipolytica mutant phenotype; strain CJM 645 on YNB-glutamate glucose, not PO1f on the Task A medium; heat shock (not modelled) raises trehalose to 7-20 nmol/mg DW",
   "trehalose_biomass_previous_term": "m294[C_cy] trehalose at 0.00686 mmol/gDW (6.86 nmol/mg DW, 2.35 mg/gDW), inherited from the source model. The same number is hard-coded without a source in the eciYali5-GEM build script (xCARBOHYDRATE); it is the iYali4 xBIOMASS trehalose share (0.0032) scaled about 2.14 times with glucan, mannan and chitin. No Yarrowia lipolytica measurement behind it was found.",
   "trehalose_biomass_scope": "Only the biomass_C trehalose term is removed; biomass_C is not re-normalised. The trehalose terms of the non-objective xBIOMASS, newBiom and R1372, the closed R1387 and R1710, and the R143 rule are unchanged.",
